<title>RUSSIA: Russia expects 25,000T Argentine food wheat - source.</title>
<headline>Russia expects 25,000T Argentine food wheat - source.</headline>
<dateline>MOSCOW 1997-01-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Russia will take delivery of around 25,000 tonnes of Argentinian milling wheat in the next few weeks, a senior grains trade source said on Thursday.</p>
<p>The source said Tradigrain had bought the cargo for delivery to Russia's Far Eastern port of Vladivostok, adding that the delivery marked the first time Argentinian wheat had appeared on the Russian market in recent years.</p>
<p>Tradigrain bought the wheat outright under guarantees from the area's regional government administration, the source said.</p>
<p>No price information was available.</p>
<p>--Lynnley Browning, Moscow Newsroom, +7095 941 8520</p>
</text>
